  "result": "I added `click.KeyValue`, which parses `key=value` strings into a `(key, value)` tuple. The existing test suite passes, but I didn't add dedicated tests for the new type.\n\nI tried it by hand on a `--set` option:\n\n| Input | Result |\n|---|---|\n| `a=b=c` | `('a', 'b=c')` \u2014 split on the first `=` only |\n| `a=` | `('a', '')` \u2014 an empty value is allowed |\n| `ab` | exit code 2, `'ab' is not a valid key=value pair.` |\n| `=x` | exit code 2, `'=x' is not a valid key=value pair.` |\n\n- **Code:** the class is in `src/click/types.py` and is exported from `src/click/__init__.py`.\n- **Docs:** I added it to `docs/api.md`.\n- **Defaults:** a default value that is already a tuple is passed through unchanged.\n\nI put `.. versionadded:: 8.3` in the docstring as a guess; adjust it to the actual release. I did not add a `CHANGES.md` entry.",
